    "result_text": "The suite is green. The full build succeeded with all tests passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for owner creation, following the codebase's established pattern for derived read-only fields (like `contactPreference`/`locality`).\n\n**Contract (`openapi.yml`)**\n- Added `birthDate` (optional ISO `date`) to `OwnerFields` \u2014 the request input.\n- Added `ageBand` (readOnly enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to `Owner` \u2014 the response output.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 `birthDate` must survive to GET time so the band can be computed:\n- Added a `birthDate` field/column to the `Owner` entity (`model/Owner.java`).\n- Added `birth_date DATE` to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Derivation logic** \u2014 a small single-responsibility unit mirroring `ContactPreference`:\n- New `util/AgeBand.java`: a pure function `of(Owner)` computing years via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)` \u2192 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+); `null` when no birth date.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `OwnerMapper` now maps `ageBand` at response time via an `ageBand(owner)` default method, exactly like the other derived fields. MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` from the request DTO into the entity by name (no request-handling YAML or new function classes needed \u2014 the spec is met entirely by the DTO round-trip plus the derivation).\n\nThe band is measured **against `registrationDate`** (the resolved/business-day-adjusted value stored on the entity), as specified. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
